# Rust engine versioning

Index: [changelog](./changelog.mdc) (app releases) · [rust-migration](./rust-migration.mdc)

The Rust engine has its **own** semver. It is **not** the app version (`apps/forja` / `kReleaseCodename` / `vX.Y.Z` tags).

**Current engine version:** `1.2.67`

---

## Source of truth

| Field | File | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| **Engine version** | [`crates/Cargo.toml`](../../crates/Cargo.toml) → `[workspace.package] version` | Only place to bump. Crates use `version.workspace = true`. Boot string is `env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")` via `ffi_version`. |
| **Dart bridge label** | [`packages/rust/pubspec.yaml`](../../packages/rust/pubspec.yaml) `version:` | Keep **identical** to workspace version in the same PR. Not what boot prints; drift confuses. |

When the version changes, update **Current engine version** above in the same PR. Dev docs may say `Rust engine v1.2.67` as a smoke example; prefer “matches workspace version” if the line will go stale.

---

## When to bump (same PR as the engine change)

| Bump | Trigger |
|------|---------|
| **patch** (`1.2.67` → `1.2.68`) | Bug fix, unlock/headers, crash, behavior fix on existing FFI surface |
| **minor** (`1.2.x` → `1.3.0`) | New FFI / new crate capability; host still works on old symbols |
| **major** (`1.x` → `2.0.0`) | Breaking FFI — deleted/renamed symbols, required host change |

Bump in the PR that lands the change. Do **not** wait for the app release workflow.

No bump for: docs-only, comment-only, `packages/rust` Dart glue that does not change Rust, or host-only Dart.

---

## What not to do

| Forbidden | Why |
|-----------|-----|
| Tie engine bump to `bump_version.sh` / app `v*` tag | App and engine ship on different clocks; engine is embedded in the binary |
| Invent `engine-v*` git tags (unless we ship a standalone dylib later) | Engine is not a separate download today |
| Edit per-crate `version =` instead of workspace | Breaks single SoT |
| Bump app `pubspec` because crates changed | App patch is a separate admin decision |
| Leave `packages/rust` pubspec behind workspace | Two “engine versions” in the tree |

---

## User-facing notes

If the change is user-visible, add/edit a bullet in the active app [`docs/changelog/*-[draft].md`](../../docs/changelog/) under **Sources**, **Player**, or **Live & IPTV** — same turn as code ([changelog](./changelog.mdc)). No separate engine changelog until we ship the engine as its own artifact.

---

## Checklist (engine PR)

1. Bump `[workspace.package] version` in `crates/Cargo.toml`
2. Match `packages/rust/pubspec.yaml` `version:`
3. Update **Current engine version** in this rule
4. Rebuild (`./scripts/build_rust.sh` or CI) so boot log shows the new `Rust engine v…`
5. Changelog bullet if users would notice
